Facility Wardens, Area Wardens and First Aid Responders
(4)
Facility Wardens, Area Wardens and First Aid Responders are responsible for:
Conducting an orderly evacuation of the facility’s occupants, including members of the public; who may be in the facility at the time; to a safe place of assembly; or
Managing emergency circumstances such as a medical response, hazardous material release or facility lock down;
Assisting with the evacuation of disabled person/s to a safe place;
Assisting during an emergency to provide First Aid, where required;
Assisting Emergency Services with emergency information;
Undertaking reporting and debrief with the view to continuous improvement.

Managers and Leaders
(5)
Managers and Leaders are responsible for
Ensuring that Facility and/or Area Wardens are appointed and role coverage is maintained;
Leading by example to provide visible support for the drill evacuations;
Managing team members and ensuring active participation during drill evacuations;
Enabling Wardens and First Aid Responders to meet their operational and training commitments.

Health & Safety Team
(7)
The Health & Safety Team are responsible for:
Providing oversight and monitoring this Procedure;
Communicating the structure of the ECO and vacancies as these arise;
Managing the training and re-fresher training for the ECO;
Coordinating the drill evacuations and including complexity to some scenarios;
Periodically acting as an independent observer and provide feedback on drill evacuations to the ECO;
Reporting on the ECO performance to the Safety Campus Group and Consultative Committees;
Reviewing the drill evacuation reports and share learnings with the University community;
Monitoring to ensure any necessary corrective actions are implemented.

All Staff, Students, and Contractors
(8)
All Staff, Students, and Contractors are responsible for:
Identifying the need for a personal evacuation plan where disability is a barrier to active participation;
Actively participating in drill evacuations and in emergencies;
Following the instructions provided by the Area Wardens and Emergency Services;
Assembling at the nominated assembly area;
Not returning to the facility or area until Emergency Services declares it safe to do so.

Part C - Drill Evacuation
(14)
All facilities under the control of La Trobe University will undertake a minimum of one drill evacuation each calendar year in alignment with Australian Standard 3745 2010. Low risk facilities with low complexity, low occupancy and minimal student interface will undertake one evacuation drill. Higher risk facilities with complexity that includes staff and student occupancy will undertake two evacuation drills; once per semester. This is to ensure there is adequate practise occurring across these dynamic occupancy settings. The drill evacuations will also endeavour to include scenario complexity to stress test the ECO structure and its performance.
(15)
Each Facility Warden will:
Prepare personal emergency evacuation plan/s as required for occupant/s with a disability;
Coordinate the drill evacuation in consultation with the Health & Safety team;
Undertake the drill evacuation, including the evacuation of people with a disability to a safe place;
Conduct a debrief after each drill evacuation;
Complete the drill evacuation report.
(16)
Each Area Warden will:
Implement emergency response process for their floor or area;
Assist the evacuation of people with a disability to a safe place;
Direct groups to the nominated assembly area;
Participate in a de-brief after each drill evacuation.
